-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ט/3 — עדכון תוספת 2008 לעובדי הוראה המועסקים בבעלויות (14.12.2008)
-- On the Treasury's letter of 7.12.2008: "תוספת 2008", the public-sector
-- supplement of section 4 of the 24.1.2008 agreement, is completed to 3%
-- from 1.12.2008 — computed as 2.88% of the current combined salary and
-- תוספת 2001 — and supplements 94 and 87 become 144.82 and 161.05.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `עדכון תוספת 2008`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (14.12.2008), addressee, and the recital: further to circular תשס"ח/4, "תוספת 2008" is to be completed to 3%, on the deputy wage commissioner's letter of 7.12.2008; the rule is §§1–4.

-- Time in this file is counted in salary months from December 2008 (0);
-- December's salary-and-indemnity statement (שכל"מ 12/08) is paid in
-- January 2009 (1).
`January 2009` MEANS 1

§§ `1`

-- §1: section 4 of the agreement of 24.1.2008 completes the public-sector
-- supplement ("תוספת 2008") to 3% from 1.12.2008; ¶2: the agreement also
-- sets that the supplement is computed, and the shekel supplements updated,
-- on the salary components at their December 2007 value, so not also on
-- the 4% erosion rise paid in January 2008.
@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p2
GIVEN `salary components at their December 2007 value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement as the agreement sets it` `salary components at their December 2007 value` IS
    `the supplement from 1.12.2008` TIMES `salary components at their December 2007 value`

`the supplement from 1.12.2008` MEANS 3%
`the erosion rise of January 2008` MEANS 4%

§§ `2`

-- §2: as so agreed, the supplement may be computed as 3% divided by 1.04 —
-- printed as 2.88% — of the combined salary and תוספת 2001 at their
-- current value.
@ref akn:art_2 akn:art_2/p2
@export The "2008 supplement" from 1.12.2008 for a teaching employee of an owning body, as circular 2008-09/3 computes it
GIVEN `current combined salary and supplement 2001` IS A NUMBER @desc the combined salary plus תוספת 2001 at their current value (after the 4% rise of January 2008)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement as the circular computes it` `current combined salary and supplement 2001` IS
    `the rate on current values` TIMES `current combined salary and supplement 2001`

`the rate on current values` MEANS 2.88%

-- §2's own arithmetic: 3% / 1.04 is 2.8846…%, printed to two decimals
-- (rounded half up, convention rounding.half).
`3% over 1.04, to two decimals of a percent, is 2.88%` MEANS
    TRUNC (`the supplement from 1.12.2008` DIVIDED BY (1 PLUS `the erosion rise of January 2008`) TIMES 100 PLUS 0.005) 2
    EQUALS 2.88
#ASSERT `3% over 1.04, to two decimals of a percent, is 2.88%`

§§ `3`

-- §3: accordingly, the supplement of agreement 94 is 144.82 and the
-- supplement of framework agreement 87 is 161.05, from 1.12.2008.
@ref akn:art_3
GIVEN s IS A `shekel supplement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount from 1.12.2008` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `supplement of agreement 94` THEN 144.82
    WHEN `supplement of framework agreement 87` THEN 161.05

DECLARE `shekel supplement` IS ONE OF
    `supplement of agreement 94`
    `supplement of framework agreement 87`

§§ `4`

-- akn:art_4/p1 A pointer: the other rules on "תוספת 2008" are in section 4 of the agreement of 24.1.2008, not restated here.

-- ¶2: the owning bodies apply the update above to their employees on the
-- teaching-employees grading, with effect from 1.12.2008 (an effective
-- date, not a deadline); ¶3: the Ministry indemnifies them for this
-- supplement in the statement for 12/08 (שכל"מ), paid in January 2009.
@ref akn:art_4/p2 akn:art_4/p3
GIVETH A DEONTIC `update party` `update action`
DECIDE `the update is applied and indemnified` IS
    PARTY `the owning bodies`
    MUST  `apply the update to teaching-grade employees with effect from 1.12.2008`
    HENCE PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
          MUST  `indemnify the owning bodies for this supplement`
          WITHIN `January 2009`
          LEST  BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 4: the Ministry indemnifies the owning bodies in the 12/08 statement, paid in January 2009"

DECLARE `update action` IS ONE OF
    `apply the update to teaching-grade employees with effect from 1.12.2008`
    `indemnify the owning bodies for this supplement`

DECLARE `update party` IS ONE OF
    `the owning bodies`
    `the Ministry of Education`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_03-a: even where the current value is exactly the December
-- 2007 value raised by 4%, 2.88% of it is 299.52 on a December 2007 base of
-- 10,000 — not the 300 the agreement's 3% gives.
`2.88% of the current value is not 3% of December 2007's` MEANS
    NOT (`the supplement as the circular computes it` (10000 TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion rise of January 2008`))
         EQUALS `the supplement as the agreement sets it` 10000)
#ASSERT `2.88% of the current value is not 3% of December 2007's`
#ASSERT `the supplement as the circular computes it` 10400 EQUALS 299.52
#ASSERT `the supplement as the agreement sets it` 10000 EQUALS 300

#TRACE `the update is applied and indemnified` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owning bodies` DOES `apply the update to teaching-grade employees with effect from 1.12.2008` AT 0
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `indemnify the owning bodies for this supplement` AT 1

§§ `Property checks`

-- §§1-2 over December 2007 bases of 1,000 to 20,000 in steps of 1,000,
-- each raised by January 2008's 4%: F-2008-09_tashsat_03-a over the whole
-- space — the circular's 2.88% of the current value falls short of the
-- agreement's 3% of the December 2007 value for every base, by 0.0048% of
-- it, and is never above it.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                LET b MEANS k TIMES 1000
                    c MEANS `the supplement as the circular computes it` (b TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion rise of January 2008`))
                    a MEANS `the supplement as the agreement sets it` b
                IN  c LESS THAN a AND a MINUS c EQUALS b TIMES 0.0048%)
            (range 1 20)

-- §3 against the same two routes. The amounts from 1.1.2007, as circular
-- תשס"ז/4 prints them (corpus circulars/2006-07_tashsaz_04, §2א-ב), are
-- used here as evidence only: 150.52 and 135.35. Raised by January 2008's
-- 4% and then by 2.88%, they give §3's 144.82 and 161.05 to the agora;
-- raised by the 4% and by 3% of their December 2007 value, as the
-- agreement words it, the framework-87 supplement is 161.06. F-a's
-- shortfall reaches §3's amounts too.
`the framework-87 supplement from 1.1.2007` MEANS 150.52
`the agreement-94 supplement from 1.1.2007` MEANS 135.35

-- Convention rounding.half (settings.toml): to the nearest agora, an exact
-- half going up (amounts here are positive).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the agora` x IS
    TRUNC (x PLUS 0.005) 2

`§3's amounts are the 2.88% route, and the 3% route parts by an agora` MEANS
        `to the agora` (`the framework-87 supplement from 1.1.2007` TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion rise of January 2008`) TIMES (1 PLUS `the rate on current values`))
        EQUALS `the amount from 1.12.2008` `supplement of framework agreement 87`
    AND `to the agora` (`the agreement-94 supplement from 1.1.2007` TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion rise of January 2008`) TIMES (1 PLUS `the rate on current values`))
        EQUALS `the amount from 1.12.2008` `supplement of agreement 94`
    AND `to the agora` (`the framework-87 supplement from 1.1.2007` TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion rise of January 2008` PLUS `the supplement from 1.12.2008`))
        EQUALS 161.06
#ASSERT `§3's amounts are the 2.88% route, and the 3% route parts by an agora`
